From c58c65ac53382f97d4bcfb712cfc0d0a7daff1fb
Subject: bevy_text: evict the faces of removed Font assets from the cosmic font system
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/c58c65ac53382f97d4bcfb712cfc0d0a7daff1fb
Date: 2026-09-14T18:36:33+01:00

Fonts enter fontdb when a span first uses them and were never removed, so
every font ever loaded stayed resident for the life of the app and remained
a candidate in glyph fallback. Remove the face when its Font asset is
dropped, and rebuild the FontSystem around the pruned database since its
per-face caches have no eviction api; prune the swash caches likewise.
